WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome back to the show!
-Thanks for having me again.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.400
-I love having you on the show.
I love having you.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.634
I want to talk about
your projects.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.100
I also think it's funny,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.434
every time you come on with the
"Queer Eye" group, the cast,

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.534
it's so fun, because everyone
thinks that you guys

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:16.634
just kind of live together.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.834
-It's like seven
or eight seasons in,

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:23.100
and people still think that
we live in this loft together.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.133
-Yes.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.601
-It really boggles my mind.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.701
-No, it's real. It's real.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:27.968
People go, like,
"Oh, that's normal. Yeah."

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.901
-It's a little concerning,
frankly. I don't know.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.834
But like, we were even at --
we were flying from,

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:37.367
actually, to the Emmys
from New Orleans,

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.501
when we were filming
our latest season.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.667
And someone stopped us
in the airport.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.000
And this thing that they do,
they're like,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.968
"Are you guys actually doing
an episode right now?"

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.000
And they look around to see if
there are, like, actual cameras.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.234
And it's like --
like, we're in an airport.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.501
Like, we're all
wearing sweatpants.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:52.534
-Yeah, no, they're like,

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:53.934
"Oh, wait,
are you surprising me?"

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.167
-Yeah, exactly.
-"With a makeover?

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.000
Let's go!"
-It's so bizarre.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.200
-By the way, you probably
came back from the Emmys

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.100
with an Emmy, 'cause you won
another Emmy since I saw you.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.400
Congratulations.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.634
-I want to talk Halloween,

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.300
because you and your partner,
Kevin,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.100
have some awesome
Halloween costumes.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.734
And here's one from
one year ago. You go all-out.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.434
This one, you were Blockbuster
back from the dead.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:24.667
-Okay, so --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.767
-I have to fully give credit --

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:27.968
He's sitting somewhere here.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.000
-Kevin?
-Fully credit to Kev.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.367
Kev is beyond --

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.567
he has a deep, pathological
obsession with Halloween.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:38.801
October 1st, I start getting
texts during his work breaks.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.100
Not while he's working.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.334
Where he starts --
-Busted.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:44.234
-He starts like trying to,
like, figure out

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.501
what we're gonna wear.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.434
We have a few that we're kind of
like, short-listing.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.601
And then we have --

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.467
So, one of them, we were
both obsessed as kids

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.467
with "Calvin and Hobbes."

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.901
-Oh, yeah, of course.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.234
-And he's 6'3", so he can be
Hobbes, and I can be Calvin.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:57.801
-Okay.
-So that was one.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:58.934
-I like that.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.567
-Another one was
the tethers from "Us."

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:04.868
Jordan Peele.
-Yes. What would --

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.234
-Creepy and kind of like scary,
with the faces and everything.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.901
-Yeah, okay, good.
-Another one was Bert and Ernie.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.300
But I feel like
that's kind of been done.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.534
Like, are they roommates?

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.267
[ Applause ]

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.801
-And...

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.033
-"Are they roommates?"

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:19.634
-There's one that I
think we're gonna go for,

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.000
but can I whisper it
in your ear?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.334
Because we don't want to share
it with everybody,

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.701
because we want it to be,
like, a surprise.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.534
-Quest, can you just play --
give us some music here?

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.934
[ Music playing ]
-Okay.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:34.000
♪♪

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.634
-Yeah, that's good, yeah.
-Is that it?

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.400
-Yeah, that's it, but you --
-Kev, we have a winner.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.200
Are we gonna get
a lot of hate?

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.200
-Yes. You'll be in a lot of
trouble, but it's very funny.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.801
Yeah, yeah, good.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.267
I was doing
a little research on you.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.868
I found out that you were in a
band called the Silver Spoons.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:53.534
When was this?
And talk to me about it.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.501
-Okay.
-And I wish I had --

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.701
Your face is getting red right
now just thinking about it.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:01.868
-So, the band lasted maybe about
one semester in college.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.400
And we were so horrible.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.601
Like, we were basically --

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.334
we were obsessed with
the Strokes and Jet

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.267
and Block Party and
Black Rebel Motorcycle Club.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:10.968
-Oh, yeah.
-And Richard Ashcroft and Oasis.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:12.601
So we, like, --
we wanted to just be them.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.534
We had the long, greasy hair
that we never washed.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:15.601
-Yes.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:16.534
-The ripped jeans
and the cowboy boots.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:17.901
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.868
-And "Silver Spoons"?
-Silver Spoons.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:21.133
-Silver Spoons.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.133
-Because we were born with,
like, silver spoon.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:24.234
It's so cringe!

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:25.934
[ Applause ]

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.767
We never played a single show.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.467
-I go, "Do you have
any lyrics or anything?"

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.868
And you found some lyrics.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.467
-Okay.
-Is this gonna --

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.234
-So, I literally went --

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.801
I have this journal
that my sister got me

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.234
that I've literally had since --

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:43.701
since before May 20th, 2004.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:46.167
Where I would just write about
my existential angst

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.400
and trying to
figure out my life.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.534
And I wrote a song

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.834
that I thought was
so clever at the time.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.601
And it's called "Jackie."
-Ooh.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.367
-And it was like,

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.501
"Am I writing about a girl
or a bottle of Jack Daniels?"

00:03:57.501 --> 00:04:00.100
I even drew a bottle of Jack
on the side.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.300
Like it's so -- it's so cringe.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.400
-"Jackie."
Can I just hear a couple lyrics?

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.567
-Yeah.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.534
"Hey, Jackie, I see you up
behind the bar.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.100
Don't hide, 'cause I can see
exactly where you are."

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.701
Like, that sounds predatory.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.801
"Come to me, don't run, 'cause
you won't get very far."

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:18.968
Okay, that's --

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:19.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.367
That didn't age well.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.901
-Yeah, it's about Jack Daniels,
but it could be about Jackie.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:26.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.467
Thank you for doing that.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.601
-This is my gift to you.
-Thank you for doing that.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.167
I will never show anyone
the full lyrics.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.133
But this is awesome,
that you trust me this much.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:35.400
Let's talk about your new hit
show, "Easy-Bake Battle."

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.968
-Yes.
-It's loosely based --

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.334
-Things that I'm
not embarrassed about.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:39.367
--- on the Easy-Bake Oven.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.367
-Yes.
-I think it's brilliant.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:44.767
And the show features a lot of
hacks, which I'm into.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:48.133
As someone who cooks,
do you know a lot of hacks

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.634
that you want to share
with the world or...?

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.200
-I feel like there are so many
hacks that I use that,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.834
you know,
chefs use traditionally

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.467
that I notice that
home cooks are using now

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.467
on TikTok,
that are coming up.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:01.934
Like, we had peeling ginger with
a spoon to remove the skin

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.100
instead of cutting it off,

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.234
so you, like,
lose too much of the flesh.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:05.267
-I didn't know that.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:06.801
-You can
microwave a potato and make

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:09.200
amazing mashed potatoes,
which I had no idea about.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.701
-Really?
I don't know about that either.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:11.634
-Right?
-No.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:12.868
-If you burn yourself --

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.634
My father taught me this,
He's a physician.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.901
I think it's a fact.
Let's just go with it.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.234
Dads -- When are dads wrong?

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.567
If you burn yourself,
the coldest part of your body

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.133
is actually your ear lobe,

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.501
because there's
the least amount of circulation.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:24.767
So, you can cool yourself off.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.000
Because you often burn yourself,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.300
if you touch something
with your index finger.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.000
So, you can cool yourself off
with your ear lobe.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.667
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.968
-This is what I'm talking about.
This is the hacks we want.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:33.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.133
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.701
This is "Easy-Bake Battle."
Take a look.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:41.067
-All you need is sushi rice,
a little bowl of water,

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.667
a selection of
literally whatever you want,

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:47.100
ice cube tray with Saran wrap.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.067
You get it already.
-I'm done.

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:50.434
I never thought of this.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:51.767
-And a little scoop as well.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:54.734
Just put in whatever elements
you want into the bottom.

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:58.634
So, then, this scoop gives you
the perfect amount of rice.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.234
And then what I do
is just wet my fingers,

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:02.434
because you don't want those
little grains to stick.

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.334
And then just press it in.

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:07.734
And the best thing about this,
it's literally ready.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.434
♪♪

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.767
-Cute.

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:13.934
Oh, my God.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on!

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:17.434
Instant sushi? Come on!
-Isn't that cute?

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:18.734
-Yes, I love that.
-Yeah!

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.100
-Antoni Porowski.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.133
"Easy-Bake Battle" is streaming
on Netflix right now!

